Z||000010||87ECO5||06-18-2000||10:48 PM||||OK - I've started doing my rims (same as Dale's).  I got all of the clearcoat and paint stripped off but now I'm noticing a discoloration in the areas where the charcoal paint was.  The discoloration is brown in color, similar to a stain left by brake dust.<P>Any suggestions for removing it?||||reg||5
Z||000011||Oreif||06-18-2000||11:02 PM||||85ECO5 ~ to remove the "stained" areas I used a small brass detail brush (brass won't damage the aluminum) and some acetone. You could probably use rubbing alchohol or paint thinner too.||||reg||1
